  "summary": "The local daemon exposes a REST API on port 8080 (machine create/list/get/delete, branch, and a /tty WebSocket with binary frames) plus an open /healthz endpoint. An MCP server package (nehemiah-mcp) lets clients like Claude Desktop and Cursor spin up and drive Nehemiah computers as a tool, configured via npx with a NEHEMIAH_URL env var. Evidence coverage: 110 of 179 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
